{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cguc6GH2DYaJDfEVqiwgW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`. It hasn't been run or validated against Camel 4.22. It receives pick lists on `direct:pick-list` and sends each one to a single `sftp` endpoint:\n\n- **Host and directory:** `sftp:warehouse.trailhead.example//inbound/picklists`. The double slash makes `/inbound/picklists` an absolute path. With one slash, Camel would treat it as a folder inside the `trailhead` user's home directory.\n- **Login:** `username: trailhead`, and `password: \"{{warehouse.password}}\"`, which Camel fills in from the property.\n- **Temporary file name:** `tempPrefix: .inprogress-`. The file is uploaded as `.inprogress-<name>` and renamed to its real name only when the upload is complete, so the warehouse never sees a half-written file.\n- **Existing files:** `fileExist: Fail`. If a file with the same name is already there, the upload fails with an error. Camel checks the real file name, not the temporary one.\n- **Host key checking:** `strictHostKeyChecking: \"yes\"`. The quotes are needed because otherwise YAML reads `yes` as the boolean `true` instead of the text \"yes\".\n\n**Before you deploy:** with strict checking on, the connection will fail unless the warehouse's host key is already known. By default Camel looks in the user's `~/.ssh/known_hosts` file. If the key is stored somewhere else, add `knownHostsFile` (a file path) or `knownHosts` (the key itself) to the endpoint."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1435,"cache_read_input_tokens":4589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1435},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pa